+# Deploying the Tip Jar (static site on IPFS, contract on Base)
+
+The site is a fully static Next.js export (`packages/nextjs/out/`) served from IPFS. It has no server. All reads and writes go from the user's browser to Base.
+
+Production build configuration (already in the repo):
+
+| What | Where |
+| --- | --- |
+| `output: "export"`, `trailingSlash: true`, `images.unoptimized` when `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true` | `packages/nextjs/next.config.ts` |
+| Target network: `chains.base` when `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true`, local fork otherwise | `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts` |
+| USDC (Base) contract entry | `packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts` |
+| Absolute OG/Twitter image URLs from `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL` | `packages/nextjs/utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts` |
+| Build guard: IPFS build fails if there is no Base (8453) TipJar in `deployedContracts.ts` | `packages/nextjs/next.config.ts` |
+| Node 25+ `localStorage` polyfill, loaded by the `build`/`dev` scripts | `packages/nextjs/polyfill-localstorage.cjs` |
+
+All `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are **baked into the bundle at build time**. You must rebuild to change them, and anyone can read them in the published site.
+
+## 0. Prerequisite: TipJar deployed on Base (once)
+
+The site reads the TipJar address for chain `8453` from `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts`. Without it, the IPFS build stops with `No Base (8453) TipJar in contracts/deployedContracts.ts`. This step uses a real key and real ETH on Base. It is **not** part of the site upload.
+
+```bash
+yarn account:import                                  # or: yarn generate — creates a keystore; fund it with a little ETH on Base
+TIP_RECIPIENT=0xYourRecipientAddress \
+  yarn deploy --network base --keystore <keystore-name>
+git add packages/foundry/broadcast/Deploy.s.sol/8453 packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts
+git commit -m "deploy TipJar to Base"
+```
+
+`TIP_RECIPIENT` is required on Base (the deploy script reverts with `RecipientRequired()` if it's missing). The recipient is immutable. Check the deployment:
+
+```bash
+TIPJAR_BASE=$(jq -r '.transactions[] | select(.contractName=="TipJar") | .contractAddress' \
+  packages/foundry/broadcast/Deploy.s.sol/8453/run-latest.json)
+cast call $TIPJAR_BASE "usdc()(address)"      --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org   # 0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913
+cast call $TIPJAR_BASE "recipient()(address)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org   # your TIP_RECIPIENT
+grep -A2 "8453: {" packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts                   # TipJar entry exists
+```
+
+## 1. Build
+
+Replace the domain with the real one. Use your own Alchemy key: the SE-2 default is shared and rate-limited. The key ends up public in the bundle, so add an allowlist for the site's domain in the Alchemy dashboard.
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+rm -rf .next out                                    # ALWAYS start clean: prevents shipping a stale build
+
+NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL="https://tipjar.yourname.eth.link" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY="<your-alchemy-key>" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID="<your-walletconnect-project-id>" \
+  yarn build
+```
+
+Don't set `NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR`: a type error should fail the production build.
+
+## 2. Verify the build before uploading
+
+Run from `packages/nextjs`:
+
+```bash
+# Every route is a directory with index.html (needed by IPFS gateways)
+ls out/index.html out/debug/index.html
+
+# OG image is absolute and points at production, not localhost
+grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>' out/index.html      # → https://tipjar.yourname.eth.link/thumbnail.jpg
+grep -c "localhost:3000" out/index.html                        # → 0
+
+# The Base TipJar address is in the bundle (case-insensitive)
+TIPJAR_BASE=$(jq -r '.transactions[] | select(.contractName=="TipJar") | .contractAddress' \
+  ../foundry/broadcast/Deploy.s.sol/8453/run-latest.json)
+grep -ril "${TIPJAR_BASE#0x}" out/_next/static/chunks | head -1                # → at least one file
+
+# Not stale: output must be newer than the latest source change
+stat -f '%Sm' app/page.tsx app/_components/*.tsx out/index.html   # macOS; Linux: stat -c '%y'
+
+# Local preview of the exact files that will be uploaded (talks to real Base)
+python3 -m http.server 8080 -d out                                 # open http://localhost:8080
+```
+
+In the preview, check that the network is **Base**, the tip feed and total load, and the "Tips go to" address is the Base recipient.
+
+## 3. Upload to IPFS (BuidlGuidl IPFS)
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+yarn bgipfs upload config init -u https://upload.bgipfs.com -k <BGIPFS_API_KEY>   # once; writes ipfs-upload.config.json (gitignored)
+yarn bgipfs upload out                                                           # prints the CID — save it
+```
+
+Record the CID, for example in the release notes. **If the CID is the same as the last deploy, you uploaded the same files**: rebuild from step 1.
+
+## 4. Post-deploy verification
+
+```bash
+CID=<cid from step 3>
+GW="https://$CID.ipfs.dweb.link"               # subdomain gateway (needs CIDv1 bafy…): site served at root, like on ENS
+# (path gateway for sharing: https://community.bgipfs.com/ipfs/$CID/)
+
+for route in / /debug/; do
+  echo "$route $(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -L "$GW$route")"   # → 200 each
+done
+
+# JS assets resolve (absolute /_next/ paths)
+ASSET=$(curl -sL "$GW/" | grep -o '/_next/static/[^"]*\.js' | head -1)
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "$GW$ASSET"                    # → 200
+
+# Title + OG metadata
+curl -sL "$GW/" | grep -o '<title>[^<]*'                                    # → USDC Tip Jar
+curl -sL "$GW/" | grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>'                 # → production URL
+
+# Same bytes as the local build
+curl -sL "$GW/" | diff -q - out/index.html && echo "index.html matches"
+```
+
+Then in a browser, on the gateway URL: connect a wallet, confirm it asks to switch to **Base**, and confirm the feed and total match what's on-chain:
+
+```bash
+cast call $TIPJAR_BASE "tipCount()(uint256)"    --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org
+cast call $TIPJAR_BASE "totalTipped()(uint256)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org   # 6 decimals
+```
+
+Only send a real tip if you mean to: on Base it moves real USDC.
+
+## 5. (Optional) Point an ENS name at the CID
+
+In the ENS app, set the content hash of `tipjar.yourname.eth` to `ipfs://<CID>` (Records → Edit → Other → Content Hash). Then verify:
+
+```bash
+NAME=tipjar.yourname.eth
+RESOLVER=$(cast call 0x00000000000C2e074eC69A0dFb2997BA6C7d2e1e "resolver(bytes32)(address)" \
+  $(cast namehash $NAME) --rpc-url https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com)
+cast call $RESOLVER "contenthash(bytes32)(bytes)" $(cast namehash $NAME) \
+  --rpc-url https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com                            # encodes your CID
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://$NAME.link/"          # → 200 (gateway cache: 5–15 min)
+curl -sL "https://$NAME.link/" | grep -o '<meta property="og:image"[^>]*>'
+```
+
+## Rules
+
+- After **any** code change: `rm -rf .next out`, then rebuild. Never upload an old `out/`.
+- A new CID for every real change. An unchanged CID means stale output.
+- Known limit: the production feed reads `Tip` events with `eth_getLogs` in 500-block batches, starting at the deploy block. Base makes about 1.3M blocks a month, so every visit re-scans all of that history and the first load gets slower each week. That's fine right after launch. Move the feed to an indexer (see the `ponder` skill) before the jar is weeks old. A dedicated `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` is mandatory, not optional.
